        <body>
            <div xml:id="d444">

                <pb facs="0792" n="698" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg698"/>

                <head>No. 444.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Manning.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-03-30"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 30,
                        1887</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 70.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In connection with my No. 47, of the 10th
                    ultimo, relative to the alleged discrimination against the United States
                    carrying trade, I now <pb facs="0793" n="699" xml:id="pg699"/> inclose a copy of
                    a farther letter from Messrs. F. Alexandre &amp; Sons, dated the 25th instant,
                    respecting the subject, and inquiring what progress has been made concerning it.
                    The Department would greatly regret to And that any differential customs duties
                    were actually enforced in Mexico which would constrain this Government to
                    execute the statutes applicable to the case of any discriminating duties or
                    import being ascertained to exist in a foreign country to the disfavor of our
                    carrying flag and the favor of the flag of such country or of any third
                    power.</p>
                <p>Awaiting your formal report, I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d444-a1.xml" xpointer="d444-a1"/>
